F1 / fig-74 / PASS
- Native pixels independently show a cropped left strip narrower than a
  half-cell, preceding the x=-1 lattice line. The reliable complete
  lattice is x=-1..4, ten half-unit columns and nineteen rows.
- f74-grid now has bounds [-1,9,4,-0.5], steps 0.5/0.5, offsets 0/0.
  f74-grid-dimensions asserts columns=10, rows=19 and is mapped by
  f74-source-grid with requires=["gridDimensions"].
- f74-border uses left x=-1.4. The grid and curve inventories expressly
  identify it as a modern partial-edge regularization, not an exact
  printed coordinate or an eleventh complete source column. The former
  stronger source-domain/complete-cell claim is no longer used there.
- Seventeen f74-partial-left-* segments at y=0.5..8.5 span -1.4..-1;
  top/bottom border and the x-axis cover the remaining boundary/axis
  ruling. The preview shows this partial strip ruled to its border.
- Only the affected left curve edge is shortened: the three sample-000
  anchors now have x=-1.4; discarded vertices/segments precede that edge.
  The first retained strokes reconnect to those anchors. Other retained
  curve objects are unchanged by the structured comparison.
- Reuse the FIRST ideal labeled-exponential/sample mathematics; no fresh
  all-sample calculation was performed. At 640px all three left endpoints
  meet the disclosed border without spill, gap or an invented marker.
  Upper steep branches still end at the intended top frame and the shallow
  branch at the right frame. Interior paths and common-point reading are
  visibly retained.

